Switch to Aggressive?
These settings replace yours in Corbanu Terminal sessions and their child
agents:
• Sandbox now: workspace-write [workdir, /tmp, $TMPDIR, /tmp/extra] (network
    access enabled); permission-request tools are off
  Aggressive: write only in the current folder: no extra writable folders, no /
    tmp or $TMPDIR; approved commands stay inside it too; escalation and
    permission-request tools are off
• Approvals now: on-request (reviewer: you)
  Aggressive: untrusted: you approve every command that is not known read-only
    (reviewer: you, never auto-review)
• Network now: on for agent commands; web search live
  Aggressive: off for agent commands; web search off
• Vault now: the vault store and sign-in file are readable to agent commands;
    secret-like environment variables are passed through (KEY, SECRET, TOKEN,
    VAULT, PASSWORD, PASSPHRASE, CREDENTIAL); shell profiles are loaded
  Aggressive: the vault store and sign-in file are unreadable to agent commands,
    and direct `corbanu vault …` commands are refused; secret-like environment
    variables (KEY, SECRET, TOKEN, VAULT, PASSWORD, PASSPHRASE, CREDENTIAL) are
    removed and shell profiles are not loaded
• Child agents now: spawned agents get this session's values
  Aggressive: spawned agents get the same values; custom roles that would change
    them are refused at start
Unchanged: model and provider, MCP servers, apps and hooks (they run outside the
sandbox), wallet scopes, and commands you have already allowed permanently (they
skip the prompt but stay sandboxed). `corbanu exec` and IDE sessions are not
covered yet.
Takes effect when you restart Corbanu Terminal; this session keeps its current
settings until then. Your config.toml is not modified.
